invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/docker-mips.sh
reason: ct_widemul_opaque's compare-carry recombination, written into
  ct_widemul, hands gcc `ll + (mid << 16)` and `hh + ...` in place of
  the ladder's sums, and at -O2 for mips32r2 the register allocator puts
  four of poly1305's sums through madd where the ladder's two are
  recorded (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/issues/122). At -Os every
  gcc keeps ct_widemul out of line, so the -Os spec reads the lone body
  at zero and passes this; only the mips32r2-gcc-O2 spec sees the
  inlined form, only Ubuntu's mips gcc can run it, and the mips lane's
  container is where that gcc runs locally. Its first step is the gate.
  The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
    uint32_t t = hl + (ll >> 16);
    uint32_t w1 = (t & 0xFFFFU) + lh;
    uint32_t hi = hh + (t >> 16) + (w1 >> 16);
    uint32_t lo = (w1 << 16) | (ll & 0xFFFFU);
    return ((uint64_t)hi << 32) | lo;
--- new
    uint32_t mid = lh + hl;
    uint32_t mid_carry = (uint32_t)(mid < lh);
    uint32_t lo = ll + (mid << 16);
    uint32_t lo_carry = (uint32_t)(lo < ll);
    uint32_t hi = hh + (mid >> 16) + (mid_carry << 16) + lo_carry;
    return ((uint64_t)hi << 32) | lo;
